To hash a 24-bit integer, you can use a simple bitwise operation to create a unique hash value. Here's a function that does that:

```javascript
function hash24bit(num) {
    return num ^ (num >>> 16);
}
```

This function uses the XOR operation to combine the lower 16 bits and the upper 16 bits of the integer, producing a unique 24-bit hash value.
